From: caoanhhao <dev@skyperry.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mm/vmalloc: export vrealloc_node_align_noprof

With CONFIG_RUST_INLINE_HELPERS the Rust helper rust_helper_vrealloc_node_align()
is inlined into the calling module, so a Rust module that uses the Vmalloc or
KVmalloc allocators (VVec, KVVec, VBox) references vrealloc_node_align_noprof()
directly. It is not exported, so such a module fails modpost:

  ERROR: modpost: "vrealloc_node_align_noprof" [drivers/gpu/nova-core/nova_core.ko] undefined!

kvrealloc_node_align_noprof() and krealloc_node_align_noprof() are exported
already; export the vmalloc variant the same way.

Signed-off-by: caoanhhao <dev@skyperry.com>
---
diff --git a/mm/vmalloc.c b/mm/vmalloc.c
index 03275beb1..a993c3775 100644
--- a/mm/vmalloc.c
+++ b/mm/vmalloc.c
@@ -4230,6 +4230,7 @@ void *vrealloc_node_align_noprof(const void *p, size_t size, unsigned long align
 
 	return n;
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(vrealloc_node_align_noprof);
 
 #if defined(CONFIG_64BIT) && defined(CONFIG_ZONE_DMA32)
 #define GFP_VMALLOC32 (GFP_DMA32 | GFP_KERNEL)
